1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 Nf6 3. e3 c5 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. Nbd2 Bg4 { This is the key move from where the next series of maneuvers start for white.Black is trying to pin the knight to the queen. Be2 is probably the most natural response from white } 6. c3 e6 7. Qa4 { This is best playable after e6 because the black light-squaed bishop can't come back to d7 to unpin the knight } 7... Bd6 { its the most natural-looking line for black, prepping for castling in the next move. But this is a mistake Nd7 or Bxf3 are the best moves for black } (7... Nd7 8. Ne5 Ndxe5 9. Bxe5 f6 10. Bg3 cxd4 11. cxd4 { no clear advantage to anyone here }) (7... Bxf3 8. Nxf3 c4 9. Ne5 { no clear advantage for anyone here either }) (7... c4 { This variation was not discussed by eric. But this looks like a reasonable option for black as well. But there are potential mistakes for black from here - see the continuation here, for example } 8. Ne5 Rc8 9. b3 cxb3 10. Nxc6 bxc6) (7... Qd7 { another variation not discussed by eric. but looks to be better for black than the lines discussed in the video } 8. Bb5 Bxf3 9. Nxf3 Qc8 10. Ne5 a6 11. Bxc6+ bxc6 12. Rc1 (12. Nxc6 { this is a mistake for white. don't take this pawn yet! } 12... Qd7)) 8. Ba6!! { apparently black loses material by force here! Taking the bishop here is a mistake for white. Stockfish rates that as a blunder/ inaccuracy } 8... bxa6 (8... Rb8 9. Bxb7 Rxb7 10. Qxc6+ { Queen is triple forking king, bishop and rook here! } 10... Qd7 11. Qxd6 Qxd6 12. Bxd6 Bxf3) (8... Bxf4 9. Bxb7 { White temporarily down a piece here. but it'll recover that soon enough. don't capture back f4 first, though!! } 9... O-O 10. Bxc6 { White will either win the rook-bishop exchange at a8 or the bishop at f3 }) (8... Qa5 { This is technically the best move for white. but could be hard to find } 9. Qxa5 Nxa5 10. Bxd6 bxa6 11. Bxc5 { White is up a pawn + has a much better pawn structure. +2.9 on engine }) 9. Qxc6+ Ke7 (9... Nd7 10. Qxd6) 10. Qb7+ Qd7 11. Bxd6+ Kxd6 12. Qxa6+ Ke7 13. Ne5 { White is up 3.2 here as per stockfish! } (13. dxc5 { White is up 3.5 here as per stockfish }) *


